WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.990
Push one domino, and a whole
line falls, one after another.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.280
Trace any event back and you find a cause.

3
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.350
And that cause was caused
by something earlier.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.410
More than seven centuries ago, the Catholic
priest and philosopher Thomas Aquinas

5
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.110
asked where such a chain could begin.

6
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.140
So does the universe itself need a cause?

7
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.390
Or could it simply be there?

8
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.060
In this mission, you'll build
Aquinas' First Three Ways,

9
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.860
one step at a time, and see
what each is meant to show.

10
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.850
Then you'll test them against
the sharpest objections,

11
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.770
starting with one
question: what caused God?

12
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: find out whether
the universe itself needs a cause.
